        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "T001 is not executable against the current tree: it says to “retain the already-applied normalization,” but `extract_params` still passes raw rustdoc names directly to `ParamName::new`, and the briefing explicitly says the transient patch was removed. An implementer could therefore leave the required importer repair absent. Explicitly require implementing/reapplying the normalization and its regression tests.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/architecture-pattern-placement-guard-realignment-2026-07-24/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 6,
              "category": "task description non-executable"
            },
            {
              "message": "T003 is mapped to IN-01, IN-02, and AC-01, but its description only specifies the Primary Adapter signature-rule change; it never requires removing or disabling the existing `DomainValueObjectInboundReferenceRequired` rule. The current evaluator and serde representation still expose that rejecting rule, while the catalogue actions attributed to T003 imply modification of `CatalogueLinterRuleKind` and `LintRuleKind`. Add the explicit rule-removal operation and corresponding regression coverage.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/architecture-pattern-placement-guard-realignment-2026-07-24/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 18,
              "category": "task-coverage gap"
            },
            {
              "message": "T007 names only “affected ADR-baseline test modules,” “CLI-composition tests,” and “all changed … paths,” without exact file or symbol targets. Because T004–T006 already own overlapping tests, the executor must invent T007's modification boundary. Name the precise test files/symbols and validation operations.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/architecture-pattern-placement-guard-realignment-2026-07-24/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 42,
              "category": "task description non-executable"
            },
            {
              "message": "Section `import-and-policy` restates the semantic-first placement behavior in prose and cites only task IDs, rather than direct upstream anchors. Replace it with concrete targets/operations plus anchors as required by `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/architecture-pattern-placement-guard-realignment-2026-07-24/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 58,
              "category": "upstream restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "Section `catalogue-enforcement` restates the narrowed structural-lint contract and its policy ordering without direct spec anchors. Reduce it to concrete targets/operations plus anchors per `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/architecture-pattern-placement-guard-realignment-2026-07-24/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 69,
              "category": "upstream restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "Section `clock-boundary` restates the upstream requirement that snapshot-time policy move into the usecase and gain an infrastructure adapter, but provides no direct anchors. Use target/operation/anchor form per `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/architecture-pattern-placement-guard-realignment-2026-07-24/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 79,
              "category": "upstream restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "Section `driver-composition-and-verification` restates the delivery-boundary, composition wiring, and external CLI behavior contract without direct anchors. Use target/operation/anchor form per `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/architecture-pattern-placement-guard-realignment-2026-07-24/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 90,
              "category": "upstream restatement"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:ea4bd41d89b23c4238a8a9af5318bdb130950ba5f9e146a6235f96269e0348d4",
          "at": "2026-07-24T11:36:17Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "T005 requires a deterministic clock-source failure test at the public `SystemClockAdapter` boundary, but the catalogue defines it as a unit type and `ClockPort::now` has no input or injectable source. Its production path obtains `chrono::Utc::now()` and converts its own valid RFC3339 output, so the named files cannot induce the required public-boundary failure without an unplanned type change or global test hook. Keep failure propagation coverage in T004's injected `ClockPort` test, or explicitly plan an authorized injection seam.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/architecture-pattern-placement-guard-realignment-2026-07-24/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 30,
              "category": "task description non-executable"
            },
            {
              "message": "T007's declared integration boundary cannot exercise the stated clock-error path: `AdrBaselineCompositionRoot` always wires the non-injectable `SystemClockAdapter`, while T007 owns only the new test file and explicitly owns no earlier source edits. A fake `ClockPort` could test interactor/driver propagation, but that would not be the declared ClockPort → SystemClockAdapter → composition path. Limit this integration task to the feasible production happy path and leave injected failure coverage in T004, or name and authorize a separate injectable test composition.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/architecture-pattern-placement-guard-realignment-2026-07-24/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 42,
              "category": "task description non-executable"
            }
          ],
